                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I bought this so so long ago, and mostly played it on a touchscreen. definitely worked well and was a lot of fun! but I took a decade of a break before finding this in my library again, and I much prefer using a controller now. I needed to alter the controller settings to be viable, but not a big deal. runs are satisfying, and it's a lot easier to make progress than I remember (which makes sense given this game continued to get beta updates 7ish years into its lifespan). I'm not a fan of the timed aspects of the game (especially without any optional meta-progression between runs) but runs tend to be quick enough because of that so things still feel fairly agile. the little summary at the end of each run is also fun/cute fwiw, I like seeing the different hero names especially for some reason. the art is also chaotic but fun, and the UI is fairly legible (especially with the different options available).\n\nI don't recall what I paid for this game in 2016, but I'm confident I got it on sale and that it was worth the small investment (especially now that I'm replaying). I'd recommend it for anyone who enjoys a run-based game and finds multitaking fun!",
